# Shared Firebase project

Web (shop dashboard) and mobile (Flutter builder app) use the **same** Firebase project: `iconstruct-58a87`. One Firestore, one Auth, one App Check, one `firestore.rules` file.

## Do

- Treat every Firestore change as affecting **both** clients
- Keep `firestore.rules` as the union of web + mobile paths. Default-deny at the bottom; every collection either app uses must be listed
- Web owns shops / billing / products. Flutter owns estimates, posts, bids, notifications, and `users/{uid}/saved_projects`
- Coordinate before adding collections or tightening rules — a mobile-only or web-only rules deploy overwrites the live file and can lock the other app out (Saved Projects `permission-denied` is the usual symptom)

## Do not

- Assume a separate Firestore for Flutter
- Deploy a rules file that only covers one client
- Register App Check debug tokens on the wrong app (use Android `com.example.iconstruct`, not a different Firebase/web app)
